                0.375
              ],
              "content": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Central\\_Park\\_A.jpgCentral park, New York City"
            }
          ],
          "image_source": "images/page_13_image_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.382,
            0.482,
            0.405
          ],
          "content": "How did they make these arches?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.409,
            0.846,
            0.448
          ],
          "content": "The first step is to be able to draw them on a plane surface such as paper or stone."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.456,
            0.595,
            0.48
          ],
          "content": "Construct this arch shape on a piece of paper."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.482,
            0.613,
            0.521
          ],
          "content": "Let us think about the support lines this figure will need."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.618,
            0.441,
            0.843,
            0.535
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_13_image_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.549,
            0.844,
            0.589
          ],
          "content": "For symmetry, we should have $\\mathrm{AB} \\equiv \\mathrm{CD}$ , and $\\angle BAD = \\angle CDA$ How would you construct these support lines?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.596,
            0.81,
            0.689
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_13_image_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.452,
            0.697,
            0.81,
            0.735
          ],
          "content": "Construct equal angles at A and D. Mark B and C such that AB = CD."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.763,
            0.846,
            0.805
          ],
          "content": "? Use these support lines to construct an arch. If required, adjust the radii of the arcs to make the arch look more aesthetically pleasing."
        },
